translation.securityRedTeaming.authorizationNotePlaceholder	e.g. link to the signed engagement, or to the bug bounty program and its scope
translation.securityRedTeaming.cancel	Cancel
translation.securityRedTeaming.confirmReject	Reject target
translation.securityRedTeaming.confirmRevoke	Revoke authorization
translation.securityRedTeaming.confirmVerify	Verify target
translation.securityRedTeaming.revokeDescription	Revoking cancels the red-team scans of {{domain}}, archives their sessions, and blocks new scans until the target is verified again.
translation.securityRedTeaming.revokeNoteLabel	Reason for revoking
translation.securityRedTeaming.revokeNotePlaceholder	e.g. authorization expired, ticket link
translation.securityRedTeaming.revokeTitle	Revoke authorization
translation.securityRedTeaming.createFailed	Couldn't add the target.
translation.securityRedTeaming.emptyDescription	Add a live domain to pentest. A Devin employee must verify authorization before a scan can run.
translation.securityRedTeaming.emptyTitle	No targets yet
translation.securityRedTeaming.launch	Launch scan
translation.securityRedTeaming.launchActiveScanWarning	A scan on this target is already queued or running. Launching another tests the same hosts in parallel and can double the traffic they receive.
translation.securityRedTeaming.launchAfterFailure	The scan you're relaunching failed: {{reason}}
translation.securityRedTeaming.launchDescription	Pentest {{domain}}. Add a repository to correlate findings against its source.
translation.securityRedTeaming.scopeSummary_one	{{first}} and {{count}} other scope entry
translation.securityRedTeaming.scopeSummary_other	{{first}} and {{count}} other scope entries
translation.securityRedTeaming.depthLabel	Scan depth
translation.securityRedTeaming.depthStandard	Standard
translation.securityRedTeaming.depthDeep	Deep
translation.securityRedTeaming.depthStandardDescription	After recon, the scan waits for you to choose which assets to test. One session then tests each.
translation.securityRedTeaming.depthDeepDescription	After recon, the scan waits for you to choose which assets to test. Up to 12 sessions then test them by vulnerability category, and up to 6 confirm and chain the best leads. Costs more.
translation.securityRedTeaming.depthUltra	Ultra deep
translation.securityRedTeaming.depthUltraDescription	Runs without waiting for you: one session hunts every discovered host, and each spawns deeper sessions for the vulnerability classes its threat model surfaces. Costs the most.
translation.securityRedTeaming.depthFoothold	Ultra deep (internal)
translation.securityRedTeaming.depthFootholdDescription	Ultra deep from inside your network: sessions run on a machine in the Outpost you choose, one at a time, and hunt everything in the scope you pick below until nothing is left open. Nothing is changed or taken down, and the scan asks you before testing anything it is not sure is yours.
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdPoolLabel	Foothold Outpost
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdPoolPlaceholder	Select an Outpost
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdPoolDescription	Sessions run as the worker's user on this machine and can read whatever that user can. Account-wide Outposts and your own personal Outposts are listed.
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdPoolRequired	Select the Outpost to test from.
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdPoolsEmpty	No Outposts are available to you in this organization.
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdPoolsFailed	Couldn't load Outposts.
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdScopeLabel	Scope
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdScopeLocalNetworks	The Outpost machine and its local networks
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdScopeReachable	Everything the Outpost machine can reach
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdScopeLocalNetworksNamed	{{outpost}} and its local networks
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdScopeReachableNamed	Everything {{outpost}} can reach
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdScopeLocalNetworksDescription	Also tests hosts on the networks the machine is directly attached to. Anything further, and any network the scan is not sure is yours, is tested only after you approve it.
translation.securityRedTeaming.footholdScopeReachableDescription	Tests every system the machine can reach that clearly belongs to your organization, through any network, VPN or internal domain. The scan pauses to ask you about anything it is not sure is yours, and about any service run by another company.
translation.securityRedTeaming.launchFailed	Couldn't launch the scan.
translation.securityRedTeaming.launchScan	Launch scan
translation.securityRedTeaming.launchSuccess	Red-team scan started.
translation.securityRedTeaming.scanTestingTitle	Devin is testing the target
translation.securityRedTeaming.scanTestingDescription	Devin is testing the target. We will show findings here as they are confirmed.
translation.securityRedTeaming.scanAwaitingInputDescription	Recon is done. Open the scan session to choose which assets Devin tests.
translation.securityRedTeaming.scanQueuedDescription	It starts automatically. We will show findings here as they are confirmed.
translation.securityRedTeaming.stopScanDescription	Devin stops testing right away. The run stays in the target's scan history with the findings it confirmed.
translation.securityRedTeaming.scanFailedDescription	Devin was unable to complete this scan. Launch a new one from this organization's Red Teaming page in the admin panel.
translation.securityRedTeaming.credentials	Credentials
translation.securityRedTeaming.authorizationNoteRequired	Justification required
translation.securityRedTeaming.revokeNoteRequired	Reason required
translation.securityRedTeaming.noteTooLong	Use {{max}} characters or fewer. This has {{length}}.
translation.securityRedTeaming.credAdd	Add credential
translation.securityRedTeaming.credAddFailed	Failed to add credential
translation.securityRedTeaming.credDelete	Delete
translation.securityRedTeaming.credDeleteTitle	Delete “{{name}}”?
translation.securityRedTeaming.credDeleteDescription	Future scans of {{domain}} won’t be able to use this credential.
translation.securityRedTeaming.credSessionClearTitle	Clear the saved login for “{{name}}”?
translation.securityRedTeaming.credSessionClearDescription	Future scans of {{domain}} won’t be able to reuse this login session. If the credential contains only the session, the credential will also be deleted.
translation.securityRedTeaming.credDeleteFailed	Failed to delete credential
